  "text": "Give something a particular form.\n\nMaking an effort to do something.\n\nM144 123 179 119 184 134 147 140Z\n\nThe time near the end of the day.\n\nAfter the expected or usual time.\n\nLater than another time or event.\n\nShows that something is possible.\n\nWrap and tighten at the next post\n\nCovered with or containing water.\n\nA person whose name is not given.\n\nHave information about something.\n\nThe time when it is dark outside.\n\nWhy something happens or is done.\n\nPutting ideas into written words.\n\nMaking a task easier for someone.\n\nNot one and not the other of two.\n\nWords that show you are grateful.\n\nIn addition; another possibility.\n\nhas not been told the arrangement\n\nTouch the sprout to help it grow\n\nNear bank at the narrow crossing\n\nSelected from the possibilities.\n\nAsks for or introduces a reason.\n\nMoved something to a later time.\n\nm178 109 10 39 25-32m-29 23 38 7\n\nSomething you have a duty to do.\n\nConnects related words or ideas.\n\nPrecisely, without a difference.\n\nHave permission to do something.\n\nMade something ready beforehand.\n\nShort for there is or there has.\n\nA word used to agree or confirm.\n\nM6 14h18M6 20h20M6 26h16M6 32h18\n\nTry docking at Grandma’s landing\n\nCarry this memory to the lantern\n\nSol’s prepared ending: the bread\n\nSecond half at the wide crossing\n\nFind or use a particular amount.\n\nExtra; kept for use when needed.\n\ngarden-studio-review g-secondary\n\nRead the choices before choosing\n\nAn edge or surface of something.\n\nWent from one side to the other.\n\nM-23-31h17v12h-17Zm29 0h18v12H6Z\n\nMoved past someone or something.\n\nDo something to develop a skill.\n\nThe inside surface above a room.\n\nPull something until it is firm.\n\nNoticed something with the eyes.\n\nAsk someone to come to an event.\n\nThe flat green parts of a plant.\n\nMoved to face another direction.",
